--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Third-party components
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

TDPdf is built as a single self-contained executable, so its dependencies are
physically inside the binary that is distributed. The complete notices - every
component, its version, its copyright line and its full licence text - are in
THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md at the root of this repository and of the source bundle,
and are embedded in the application itself under Help > Third-Party Licenses.
Regenerate that file with build/generate-third-party-notices.ps1.

Summary of what is bundled:

  Native, extracted at runtime
    PDFium (via Docnet.Core)  BSD-3-Clause, plus its own aggregate notice
                              covering libpng, LibTIFF, agg23, FreeType,
                              Little CMS, OpenJPEG, zlib, libjpeg-turbo,
                              the Independent JPEG Group and ICU
    Leptonica                 BSD-2-Clause
    Tesseract OCR engine      Apache-2.0

  Apache-2.0
    PdfPig, Tesseract (.NET wrapper), SixLabors.ImageSharp,
    SixLabors.Fonts, OpenTelemetry .NET

  MIT
    PdfSharpCore (vendored, modified), Docnet.Core, SharpZipLib,
    CommunityToolkit.Mvvm, and the Microsoft.Extensions.* / System.*
    runtime packages

Tesseract trained-data models are NOT bundled. They are downloaded from
tesseract-ocr/tessdata_fast and tessdata_best (Apache-2.0) when OCR is first
used for a language.

Every licence above is compatible with GPLv3. Note that Apache-2.0 is
compatible with GPL version 3 but NOT with GPLv2; TDPdf is GPLv3-only, so this
holds, and relicensing to "GPLv2 or later" would break it.

PdfSharpCore is vendored under third_party/PdfSharpCore/ rather than consumed
as a NuGet package, so that PDF/A conformance and rendering fixes can be
applied at the source. Local modifications are marked with a "KillerPDF patch"
or "TDPdf patch" comment; see third_party/PdfSharpCore/VENDORED.txt for the
upstream commit and third_party/PdfSharpCore/LICENSE.md for its MIT license.
The MIT license and copyright notices are preserved intact.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Privacy / telemetry
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

TDPdf does not phone home by default. Released binaries ship with no
telemetry endpoint embedded. The OpenTelemetry pipeline is initialized at
startup but operates as a no-op unless an administrator has explicitly
provisioned an OTLP collector, either through the environment variables
TDPDF_OTLP_ENDPOINT and TDPDF_OTLP_TOKEN, or through policy values at:

    HKLM\SOFTWARE\Policies\TDPdf\Telemetry\OtlpEndpoint
    HKLM\SOFTWARE\Policies\TDPdf\Telemetry\OtlpToken

The policy key is ACL'd so that only SYSTEM and BuiltinAdministrators can
modify it. Reporting can be disabled on a device at any time with:

    TDPdf.exe /clear-telemetry

That writes a sentinel which outranks every configuration source above,
including administrator-pushed policy.

When provisioned, TDPdf emits usage events (App.Startup, Tool.Selected,
File.Open/New/Save/SaveFlattened/Merge/Split/Print, Install.Start/Success,
Install.Crash, Crash) to the configured collector. File paths, file names,
document content, user names, and persistent user identifiers are not
emitted. Stack traces are scrubbed of paths before transmission. Reports
carry the machine name (host.name); no other identifying field is sent,
and the per-launch session identifier is never stored. See PRIVACY.md and
docs/intune-distribution.md for full details.

Prior to version 1.24.0.0, TDPdf could also report to Azure Application
Insights, provisioned by a DPAPI-encrypted file at
%ProgramData%\TDPdf\telemetry.dat or by a build-time-embedded key. That
destination and both provisioning mechanisms have been removed; upgrading
deletes any telemetry.dat left behind.

